// SL-221, the CROSS-MODULE half of `coro_suspending_default_omitted.saw`. The
// callee is `modules.sl208_calls.suspdefN`, whose default calls a suspending
// helper private to that module, and the omitting call is module-qualified.
//
// The pair exists to pin that the two modules answer ALIKE: same refusal, same
// wording, differing only in the callee's name. That is the SL-208 claim at the
// refusal end — before it, this spelling COMPILED and printed the right answer
// with the suspension silently dropped (0 Pending resumes under
// `__saw_drive_steps`), while the same-module spelling crashed the compiler with
// `IndexError: list index out of range`. One sentence now, in both modules.
//
// The position is EMBEDDED here, as it is in the same-module file, and that is
// forced rather than chosen: a module-qualified call cannot BE a drive or spawn
// root (SL-217), so every cross-module cell of the matrix reaches a frame
// through an entry-module wrapper like `root` below. One funnel answers every
// position (`_arity_args`), so the same-module file's root cells cover the
// entry points this one cannot reach.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: the default value of parameter `x` of `suspdefN` suspends

import modules.sl208_calls

func root() -> Int {
    sl208_calls.suspdefN()
}

func main() {
    print(__saw_drive(root()))
}
